.TH "PUBLICKEYCREDENTIAL.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
PublicKeyCredential.toJSON \- PublicKeyCredential: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]PublicKeyCredential\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable
plain object representing the \f[CR]PublicKeyCredential\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when a
\f[CR]PublicKeyCredential\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]authenticatorAttachment\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]: not present if
its value is \f[CR]null\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]clientExtensionResults\f[R]: a JSON\-serializable object
representing the values returned by
\f[CR]getClientExtensionResults()\f[R], with buffer values encoded as
base64url strings
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]id\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]rawId\f[R]: encoded as a base64url string
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]response\f[R]: a JSON\-serializable object representing the
\f[CR]AuthenticatorResponse\f[R] value, with buffer values encoded as
base64url strings.
Namely:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
When it\(cqs a \f[CR]AuthenticatorAssertionResponse\f[R], contains the
following properties:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]authenticatorData\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]clientDataJSON\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]signature\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]userHandle\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]: not present if its value is
\f[CR]null\f[R]
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
When it\(cqs a \f[CR]AuthenticatorAttestationResponse\f[R], contains the
following properties:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]attestationObject\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]authenticatorData\f[R]: the value returned by
\f[CR]getAuthenticatorData()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]clientDataJSON\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]publicKey\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]: the value returned by
\f[CR]getPublicKey()\f[R], omitted if it is \f[CR]null\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]publicKeyAlgorithm\f[R]: the value returned by
\f[CR]getPublicKeyAlgorithm()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]transports\f[R]: the value returned by \f[CR]getTransports()\f[R]
.RE
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]type\f[R]
.PP
Unless stated otherwise, each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]SecurityError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
The RP domain is not valid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
When registering a new user, a relying party server will supply
information about the expected credentials to the web app.
The web app calls \f[CR]navigator.credentials.create()\f[R] with the
received information (\f[CR]createCredentialOptions\f[R] below), which
returns a promise that fulfills with the new credential (a
\f[CR]PublicKeyCredential\f[R]).
.PP
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object.
Its properties have the same values as the corresponding properties of
the original object.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] credential = \f[B]await\f[R] navigator.credentials.create({
  publicKey: createCredentialOptions,
});

\f[B]const\f[R] json = credential.toJSON();
console.log(json); \f[I]// A plain object\f[R]
console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
console.log(json.id); \f[I]// Same value as credential.id\f[R]
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
The returned credential is serialized using \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R],
which calls the \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method automatically.
The web app posts the serialized credential back to the server.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] jsonString = JSON.stringify(credential);
console.log(jsonString);

\f[B]const\f[R] registrationURL = \(dqhttps://example.com/registration\(dq;
\f[B]const\f[R] apiRegOptsResp = \f[B]await\f[R] fetch(registrationURL, {
  method: \(dqPOST\(dq,
  headers: { \(dqContent\-Type\(dq: \(dqapplication/json\(dq },
  body: jsonString,
});
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqauthenticatorAttachment\(dq: \(dqplatform\(dq,
  \(dqclientExtensionResults\(dq: {},
  \(dqid\(dq: \(dq...\(dq,
  \(dqrawId\(dq: \(dq...\(dq,
  \(dqresponse\(dq: {
    \(dqattestationObject\(dq: \(dq...\(dq,
    \(dqauthenticatorData\(dq: \(dq...\(dq,
    \(dqclientDataJSON\(dq: \(dq...\(dq,
    \(dqpublicKey\(dq: \(dq...\(dq,
    \(dqpublicKeyAlgorithm\(dq: \-7,
    \(dqtransports\(dq: [\(dqinternal\(dq]
  },
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqpublic\-key\(dq
}
.EE
.PP
The base64url\-encoded values are abbreviated as \f[CR]\(dq...\(dq\f[R]
for readability.
